    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Inscr.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:VAtr">V Atr</ref> Inscr.</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="V Atr. Inscr." corresp="#wit-g">In nomine Do<hi rend="italic">mi</hi>ni, an<hi rend="italic">no</hi> do<hi rend="italic">mi</hi>nic<hi rend="italic">ae</hi> incarn<hi rend="italic">ationis</hi> MVIII</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="V Atr. Inscr." corresp="#wit-g2">Be Angolwitena gerednesse.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">In nomine Domini</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-d">In the name of the Lord. [G1: anno dominicae incarnationis MVIII; G2: Angolwitena gerednesse]</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">Im Namen des Herrn, im Jahre der Fleischwerdung des Herrn 1008. (Vom Beschlusse der Englischen Witan. G2)</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">In the name of the Lord, in the year of the Lord's incarnation 1008. (Of the decision of the English witan. G2)</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Base text K = G (Cotton Nero A I f. 89, after III Eg, c. 1060); N = G2 (Cotton Nero A I f. 116v, after a homily attributed to Wulfstan, c. 1070); D (CCCC 201 p. 48) is also given here. Liebermann suggests VI Atr (‘at Enham’) may be a private reworking of the draft of V Atr. G2 inserts and omits matter as in X Atr 1–2.1.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
